testify|witness|VERB|Give witness evidence|To give evidence as a witness, especially in court.|làm chứng|She was asked to testify at the hearing.|Cô ấy được yêu cầu làm chứng tại phiên điều trần.|Testify about or that; legal context varies.|0
somewhere|adverb|ADVERB|At an unspecified place|At or to a place whose exact location is not stated.|ở đâu đó; đến đâu đó|I left my notebook somewhere upstairs.|Tôi để vở ở đâu đó trên tầng.|Location adverb.|0
somewhere|pronoun|PRONOUN|An unspecified place|A place that is not named or specified.|nơi nào đó|We need somewhere quiet to talk.|Chúng ta cần một nơi yên tĩnh để nói chuyện.|Can be followed by adjective.|1
sympathetic|understanding|ADJECTIVE|Showing understanding and care|Showing that you understand and care about someone's problems.|thông cảm; đồng cảm|Her supervisor was sympathetic about the delay.|Cấp trên thông cảm với sự chậm trễ của cô ấy.|Sympathetic to or towards; false friend not pleasant.|0
stranded|stuck|ADJECTIVE|Unable to leave|Unable to leave a place because transport or another means is unavailable.|mắc kẹt|The storm left travellers stranded at the station.|Cơn bão khiến hành khách mắc kẹt ở nhà ga.|Stranded in or at.|-
seriously|earnestly|ADVERB|With serious attention|With care and attention, rather than as a joke.|nghiêm túc|Please consider the offer seriously.|Hãy xem xét đề nghị một cách nghiêm túc.|Manner adverb.|0
seriously|severely|ADVERB|To a severe degree|To a degree that is severe or important.|nghiêm trọng|The roof was seriously damaged.|Mái nhà bị hư hỏng nghiêm trọng.|Degree adverb.|1
